# Prompt
You are the speckit specification agent for EPAM CLI. Phase scaffold, story SKY-001b.
NOTE: This story has 17 acceptance criteria — MANDATORY split required (see SPLIT RULES below).

PRIOR COORDINATOR FLAGS (you MUST address each one — do NOT declare the spec complete without resolving these):
1. directed_fix_not_applied: RAPIDAPI_KEY non-empty prerequisite gate AC was explicitly assigned in coordinatorNotes for both the prior run and this run — it remains absent after two speckit passes; all probe-dependent ACs are vacuously passable when key is absent or invalid
2. directed_fix_not_applied: inferred_contract_risk flag was carried forward from prior coordinator review without resolution — human must explicitly accept that SKY-002 may build on inferred FlightResult field mappings derived solely from 429 responses and documentation
3. ac_rewrite_pattern: speckit replaced the full AC set rather than applying targeted additions as directed — this increases review surface and obscures whether the directed fixes were considered and rejected or simply missed
4. weak_ac: final RESTful conventions AC uses subjective qualifier 'where applicable' without a testable rubric — pass/fail determination is ambiguous for automated or peer verification
5. missing_failure_mode_coverage: no AC addresses what happens if all probed endpoints return 404 (i.e. no working endpoint can be documented) — the story has no defined failure/abort condition for this scenario

Additional context from prior review: The speckit agent made genuine improvements over the openspec baseline — tightening key-exposure validation (substring >4 chars threshold), adding an ordering constraint on the probe sequence, requiring the Discovery Metadata section to be machine-parseable, clarifying the 429 Sample Response handling, and hardening the Endpoints section to exclude sky-scanner3 paths from the document entirely (not just the section). These are non-trivial improvements. However, the two directed fixes explicitly 

